{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.QTraceCyclic","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.QTraceCyclic","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.IwahoriHecke.QuantumTrace"],"declarations":11,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.QuantumTrace.qTrace_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.QuantumTrace.qTrace_conj","kind":"theorem","line":180,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/QTraceCyclic.lean#L180-L197","doc":"**Conjugation-invariance.** An immediate consequence of cyclicity: `tr_w` is a class\nfunction on the Hecke algebra, so it is constant on conjugacy classes of units — in\nparticular on the braid-group images of conjugate braids, which is the Markov move I\n(conjugation) invariance the Jones polynomial needs.\n\nMarkov move II is the *peel*, and is a separate statement — see\n`QOU.IwahoriHecke.MarkovPeel`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.QuantumTrace.qTrace_mul_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.QuantumTrace.qTrace_mul_comm","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/QTraceCyclic.lean#L159-L178","doc":"**`tr_w` is cyclic.** `tr_w(x y) = tr_w(y x)` for arbitrary elements of `H_{m+1}(q)`,\nat every weight `w`.\n\nThe proof is three associativity steps around one use of the commutation and one use of the\nordinary cyclicity of the matrix trace: `tr(W X Y) = tr(X W Y) = tr((W Y) X) = tr(W Y X)`.\nThis supersedes `qTrace_sigma_mul_comm`, which is the special case `x = σ_a`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.QuantumTrace.siteWeight_comm_heckeActionN","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.QuantumTrace.siteWeight_comm_heckeActionN","kind":"theorem","line":148,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/QTraceCyclic.lean#L148-L155","doc":"The commutation, as an equation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.QuantumTrace.heckeActionN_mem_weightCentralizer","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.QuantumTrace.heckeActionN_mem_weightCentralizer","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/QTraceCyclic.lean#L137-L146","doc":"**The whole image centralises the weight.** For *every* `x`, not merely for generators. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.QuantumTrace.val_comp_heckeActionCentral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.QuantumTrace.val_comp_heckeActionCentral","kind":"theorem","line":128,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/QTraceCyclic.lean#L128-L135","doc":"Composing the corestriction back with the inclusion returns the original action. Two\nalgebra maps agreeing on the balanced generators are equal. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.QuantumTrace.heckeActionCentral_sigma","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.QuantumTrace.heckeActionCentral_sigma","kind":"theorem","line":122,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/QTraceCyclic.lean#L122-L126","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.QuantumTrace.heckeActionCentral","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.QuantumTrace.heckeActionCentral","kind":"def","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/QTraceCyclic.lean#L102-L120","doc":"**The Hecke action, corestricted to the centralizer of the weight.**\n\nThe same three obligations as `heckeActionN`, pulled back along the injective\n`Subalgebra.val`; nothing is reproved. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.QuantumTrace.strandBraid_altProd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.QuantumTrace.strandBraid_altProd","kind":"theorem","line":88,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/QTraceCyclic.lean#L88-L100","doc":"**The braid relation for the strand braidings, read off the action.**\n\nNot a new computation: `heckeActionN` already discharged this obligation, so applying it to\n`Balanced.sigma_braid` and pushing through `map_altProd` returns the matrix-level statement.\nStated separately because the subalgebra lift below needs it in this form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.QuantumTrace.strandBraid_mem_weightCentralizer","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.QuantumTrace.strandBraid_mem_weightCentralizer","kind":"theorem","line":77,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/QTraceCyclic.lean#L77-L83","doc":"Every strand's braiding centralises the weight — restating `braidAt_comm_siteWeight`\nas a membership. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.QuantumTrace.weightCentralizer","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.QuantumTrace.weightCentralizer","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/QTraceCyclic.lean#L71-L75","doc":"The centralizer of the site weight `W` inside `End(V^{⊗(m+1)})`. Everything the Hecke\naction produces lives here — that is the content of this file. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.IwahoriHecke.QuantumTrace.isHeckeGenerator_of_injective","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.IwahoriHecke.QuantumTrace.isHeckeGenerator_of_injective","kind":"theorem","line":57,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/IwahoriHecke/QTraceCyclic.lean#L57-L67","doc":"**`IsHeckeGenerator` descends along an injective algebra map.** The quadratic relation is\nan equation between algebra expressions, so an injective algebra map reflects it. This is\nwhat lets the `liftBalanced` obligations be discharged inside a subalgebra without redoing\nany of the matrix computation. ","signatureChunk":0}]}